#
# Based on meta-rockchip's wic/rockchip.wks, with one addition: a forced
# HDMI video mode on the kernel command line. This head unit's HDMI EDID
# read is intermittently unreliable (the connector reports "connected" but
# an empty mode list), which leaves DRM unable to create a framebuffer at
# all -- autoapp then crash-loops on "Cannot create window: no screens
# available" indefinitely instead of the few-seconds delay a slow-but-
# working EDID read causes. Forcing a mode means DRM always has a usable
# framebuffer regardless of whether EDID comes back.
#
# The forced mode is 1280x720@60, NOT the panel's true native 1024x600:
# the actual panel is a Waveshare WS170120 7" HDMI+USB-touch display
# (fixed 1024x600), but this board's VOP/HDMI output could not be made
# to establish ANY custom timing computed for 1024x600 -- both a
# standard CVT modeline (49.00MHz) and a reduced-blanking CVT modeline
# (43.75MHz) were tried directly via eglfs_kms.json's "mode" (with the
# connector name bug below already fixed) and both left every CRTC
# disabled (verified via /sys/kernel/debug/dri/*/state: enable=0
# active=0) -- rejected outright, not just wrong-refresh. The kernel's
# own "video=" cmdline forcing of 1024x600 was similarly ineffective:
# even with it present in /proc/cmdline, the system still ended up
# scanning out 1024x768 (this board's no-EDID fallback list). UPDATE:
# the panel's EDID *is* actually readable (128 bytes, valid) via
# /sys/class/drm/*-HDMI-A-*/edid -- an earlier claim here that it reads
# back 0 bytes was wrong (scp of that sysfs file always reads 0 bytes
# since it isn't a seekable regular file; `ssh ... cat ...` works and
# returns real data). Its decoded preferred timing (1024x600, 49.000MHz,
# 60Hz, negative sync) was tried directly against Qt's eglfs_kms "mode"
# and was ALSO rejected outright, identically to the two CVT attempts
# above and a fourth vendor-timing guess -- four structurally different,
# mathematically valid 1024x600 timings, all rejected the same way, is
# conclusive: this VOP's PLL cannot generate a 1024x600 pixel clock at
# all. It was never an EDID-detection problem.
#
# 1280x720 is used instead of that 1024x768 fallback because it's a
# true CEA-861 standard timing (unlike any hand-computed 1024x600
# modeline) that this VOP does accept, and its aspect ratio (1.778) is
# far closer to the panel's actual 1024x600 (1.707, ~4% off) than
# 1024x768's (1.333, ~28% off) -- letting the panel's own onboard
# scaler do a clean, near-uniform ~0.8x downscale in both dimensions
# instead of a badly mismatched 4:3-into-16:9.4 fit. eglfs_kms.json
# pins Qt to the exact CEA-861 720p60 modeline explicitly so autoapp's
# actual scanout resolution is guaranteed regardless of what the
# no-EDID connector fallback would otherwise pick.
#
# Disk layout
# Note that the reference documentation refers to 512 byte disk sectors, but
# wic uses 1KB blocks
#
#   Partition   Start Sector    Number of Sectors
#   loader1     64              8000
#   reserved1   8064            128
#   reserved2   8192            8192
#   loader2     16384           8192
#   atf         24576           8192
#   boot        32768           229376
#   root        262144          -           (suggested)

part loader1    --offset 32     --fixed-size 4000K            --source rawcopy                                                 --sourceparams="file=${SPL_BINARY}"
part reserved1  --offset 4032   --fixed-size 64K
part reserved2  --offset 4096   --fixed-size 4096K
part loader2    --offset 8192   --fixed-size 4096K            --source rawcopy                                                 --sourceparams="file=u-boot.${UBOOT_SUFFIX}"
part atf        --offset 12288  --fixed-size 4096K
part /boot      --offset 16384  --size       114688K --active --source bootimg-partition --fstype=vfat --label boot --use-uuid --sourceparams="loader=u-boot"
part /                                                        --source rootfs            --fstype=ext4 --label root --use-uuid

bootloader --ptable gpt --append="console=tty1 console=${RK_CONSOLE_DEVICE},${RK_CONSOLE_BAUD}n8 video=HDMI-A-1:1280x720@60 rw rootfstype=ext4 init=/sbin/init"
